From fe196cfd9705440985223c62b6865993144cb5fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Ruhier <aruhier@mailbox.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:53:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: qcom: balance runtime PM in the wakeup interrupt

The DP and DM HS PHY wakeup interrupts can fire back to back, for
instance right after the glue runtime suspends following a disconnect.
The first handler resumes xHCI, and rpm_resume() then queues an async
autosuspend for it. The second handler's pm_runtime_resume() finds
xHCI already active: rpm_resume() returns 1 without queueing an idle,
but it has cleared power.request on the way, cancelling the suspend
queued by the first handler. Nothing requests it again, so xHCI and the
glue stay runtime active, with their interconnect votes, until
something else touches runtime PM.

Take and drop a reference instead, so that each handler re-evaluates
whether xHCI can suspend. A real wakeup still keeps it active, as
xhci_resume() resumes the root hub on a pending port event.

Seen on a Lenovo Yoga Slim 7x after unplugging a USB-C monitor with a
hub: the two controllers used by it stayed active until power/control
was toggled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
index ac68b4218b56b..ca8307219e5f8 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -412,9 +412,15 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_dwc3_resume_irq(int irq, void *data)
 	/*
 	 * This is safe as role switching is done from a freezable workqueue
 	 * and the wakeup interrupts are disabled as part of resume.
+	 *
+	 * The DP and DM wakeup interrupts can fire together. A bare resume
+	 * from the second one cancels the suspend request queued after the
+	 * first one, leaving the controller active, so balance it with a put.
 	 */
-	if (dwc3_qcom_is_host(qcom))
-		pm_runtime_resume(&dwc->xhci->dev);
+	if (dwc3_qcom_is_host(qcom)) {
+		pm_runtime_get_sync(&dwc->xhci->dev);
+		pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(&dwc->xhci->dev);
+	}
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
